    when preprocessing is successful
      modifies the context

Step failure vs exception semantics
  step raises an unclassified exception (a bug)
    settles the parent as an exception, fires on_exception (not on_failure), reports exactly once
  step raises an exception it classifies as a failure via fails_on
    travels the failure path: parent failure, prefixed, no report
  step calls fail! (deliberate failure)
    settles the parent as a failure, fires on_failure (not on_exception), and does not report
  step calls done! (early completion)
    settles ok, merges exposures, and continues to the next step

